---
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import Paragraph from "./Paragraph.astro";

// The founder's note, framed as an elevated "paper" sheet so it reads as a
// letter and stands apart from the flat sections above and below it.
---

<Section id="letter" width="medium">
  <div
    class="relative bg-background dark:bg-white/[0.04] border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 sm:p-10 md:p-14 shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.05),0_18px_40px_-18px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] dark:shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.4),0_18px_40px_-18px_rgba(0,0,0,0.55),inset_0_1px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.05)]"
  >
    <!-- sr-only landmark: a letter has no title, but screen-reader heading
         nav needs one so this section isn't an unnamed landmark. -->
    <h2 class="sr-only">A note from Picmal's founder</h2>

    <!-- Founder badge: a transparent starburst cutout, so depth comes from a
         shape-following drop-shadow (a ring/box-shadow would box the star).
         Decorative → pointer-events-none + empty alt is intentional. -->
    <img
      src="/founder-badge.png"
      alt=""
      width="156"
      height="151"
      loading="lazy"
      class="pointer-events-none select-none absolute -top-6 -right-2 sm:-top-8 sm:-right-4 w-20 h-20 sm:w-24 sm:h-24 rotate-6 [filter:drop-shadow(0_6px_14px_rgba(0,0,0,0.20))]"
    />

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <Paragraph color="primary">Hello there 👋</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph color="primary">
          I'm <a
            href="https://albertogalca.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            aria-label="Alberto (opens in a new tab)"
            class="link">Alberto</a
          >, the developer behind Picmal.</Paragraph
        >
        <Paragraph color="primary">
          Picmal started because I was tired of opening a browser every time I
          needed to convert a few files. I figured there had to be a better way,
          so I built one.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph color="primary">
          Over time, that simple image converter has grown into something much
          bigger, mostly thanks to the people who use it.
        </Paragraph>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <Paragraph color="primary">
          Along the way, I've tried to stay true to a few simple ideas: your
          files should stay on your computer, the app should feel at home on
          your Mac, and you should only have to pay once.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph color="primary">
          One of my favorite parts of building Picmal is talking to customers.
          Many of the features in the app today started as conversations with
          people who needed something that didn't exist yet.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph color="primary">
          So if there's a feature you've always wished for, or something you
          haven't found in other tools, I'd love to <a
            href="mailto:support@picmal.app"
            class="link">hear from you</a
          >. If it fits Picmal, I'll do my best to build it.
        </Paragraph>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <Paragraph color="primary" class="mb-1">Best,</Paragraph>
          <!-- Deliberate off-scale exception: the handwritten signature is the
               one decorative script on the site, not part of the UI type scale.
               leading-tight (not none) so cursive descenders don't clip. -->
          <p class="font-signature text-text text-3xl leading-tight">Alberto</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
